#!/usr/bin/env python3

"""
Report PCIe link, bandwidth and power management state of PCI devices, and
flag whatever deserves a second look: links trained below what both ends
support (and what holds them back), end-to-end bandwidth bottlenecks, ASPM and
L1 substates left disabled, runtime PM switched off, latched errors.

Facts come from `lspci -vvv` -- run live, or read from a saved dump -- and,
when running live, from sysfs (runtime PM, ASPM knobs, AER counters) and the
kernel log of the current boot.

The three layers below are kept apart on purpose:
  - probe_*()    -- extraction only, no judgement
  - analyse()    -- findings over the extracted facts
  - render_*()   -- presentation
"""

